@startuml
title PayLink - Failed Payment Hold Release (Required Phase 1 Sequence)
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor Customer
participant "Payment Processing" as Payment
participant "Biller Adapter" as Biller
participant "WalletService" as Wallet
participant "PaymentEventPublisher" as Events
participant "NotificationService" as Notify
participant "AuditService" as Audit
database "PayLink Database" as DB

Biller --> Payment : Definitive refusal + reason
Payment -> DB : Persist biller outcome
Payment -> DB : Transition SentToBiller -> Failed\nappend status history
Payment -> Audit : Record failed outcome
Audit -> DB : Append audit record
Payment -> Wallet : releaseHeldFunds(paymentId) [key = paymentId/RELEASE]
Wallet -> DB : Atomic transaction: append release movement and ledger entries\nFailed -> Refunded + status history
DB --> Wallet : Release and transition committed once
Wallet --> Payment : Funds available; payment Refunded
Payment -> Audit : Record financial release (who, when, why)
Audit -> DB : Append audit record
Payment -> Events : Publish failure event asynchronously
Events ->> Notify : onPaymentEvent(FAILED)
Notify -> DB : Persist notification; deliver/retry independently
Notify --> Customer : Failure notification with reason

note over Payment,Wallet
  This is the mandatory failure workflow. The hold release is
  atomic and idempotent. Unknown payments retain their hold and
  cannot enter this flow until definitive failure evidence moves
  them to Failed.
  The hold is the full customer total, including the service fee.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
title PayLink - Proposed Optional Completed Payment Refund (FR-27; team/TA decision pending)
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor Customer
actor "Support Employee" as Support
participant "Refund API" as API
participant "RefundService" as Refund
participant "WalletService" as Wallet
participant "AuditService" as Audit
database "PayLink Database" as DB

Customer -> API : Request refund(paymentId)
API -> Refund : submitRequest(paymentId, customerId)
Refund -> DB : Verify payment exists and is Completed; create request
DB --> Refund : RefundRequest(REQUESTED)
Refund -> Audit : Record request
Audit -> DB : Append audit log
Refund --> Customer : Request pending review

Support -> API : Authorized Support-role reviewer decides with reason
API -> Refund : decide(requestId, approved, supportId, reason)
Refund -> DB : Verify REQUESTED and Completed; store reviewer, decision time and reason

alt Support rejects
  Refund -> DB : Set request REJECTED with reviewer, time and reason
  Refund -> Audit : Record outcome, actor, time, reason and payment/refund IDs
  Audit -> DB : Append audit log
else Support approves
  Refund -> DB : Set request APPROVED with reviewer, time and reason
  Refund -> Audit : Record outcome, actor, time, reason and payment/refund IDs
  Audit -> DB : Append audit log
  Refund -> Wallet : Proposed: credit customer wallet once (AQ-07/AQ-12 pending)
  Wallet -> DB : Proposed atomic wallet credit and REFUND ledger movement
  DB --> Wallet : Credit recorded once
  Wallet --> Refund : Credit successful
  Refund -> DB : Set request PROCESSED
  Refund -> Audit : Record financial processing and resulting ledger movement ID
  Audit -> DB : Append audit log
end

note over Refund,DB
  PROPOSAL ONLY — this flow does not finalize the unresolved business
  decision. The wallet-credit method and refund amount/eligibility remain
  unresolved under AQ-07. The user approved the proposed AQ-12 rule on
  2026-11-25: one authorized Support-role reviewer; audit actor, time,
  outcome, reason, payment/refund identifiers and resulting ledger movement;
  no dual control. Team/TA confirmation is still pending; this is not
  team/TA approval.
  On 2026-11-25 the user approved deferring implementation and method
  selection until team/TA resolution. This is not team/TA approval.
  FR-27 is optional and distinct from Failed -> Refunded hold release.
  The official lifecycle makes Completed terminal and lists no
  Completed -> Refunded transition. This workflow therefore records
  its own RefundRequest status and does not alter Payment.state.
  No completed-payment refund method or rule is approved by this diagram.
end note
@enduml
